<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="AZD: Pipeline metrics and agent pools" id="Azd-Pipeline-Metrics">

    <primary-label ref="azd"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Open: <control>Pipeline Metrics</control> in the <control>AZD Pipelines</control> title bar</p>
        <p>Requires: the IDE built-in browser (JCEF)</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Track pipeline pass rate, duration, queue time and failure causes, and manage the agents in your agent pools.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Pipeline pass rate, duration, queue time and failure causes, plus agent pools.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Track Azure Pipelines pass rate, build duration, queue time and failure causes in JetBrains IDEs with
        AZD, and inspect and manage agent pools and agents.</web-summary>

    <p>
        The <control>Pipeline Metrics</control> editor tab has two tabs: <control>Pipeline</control>, a dashboard of the runs in the repository,
        and <control>Agents</control>, the agent pools of the organization.
        For metrics about pull requests, see <a href="Work-with-Azure-DevOps-pull-requests.topic" anchor="pr-metrics">Pull request metrics</a>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Open the pipeline dashboard" id="pipeline-dashboard">
        <procedure title="Open pipeline metrics" id="open-pipeline-metrics">
            <step>
                <p>Open the <control>AZD Pipelines</control> tool window.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In the title bar, click <control>Pipeline Metrics</control>.</p>
                <p>The <control>Pipeline Metrics</control> editor tab opens on the <control>Pipeline</control> tab.</p>
                <img src="azd_pipeline_metrics.png" alt="Pipeline Metrics dashboard with the summary row and populated widgets for the last 90 days" width="706" thumbnail="true" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Narrow the data with the filters at the top: <control>Time range</control>, <control>Pipeline</control>,
                    <control>Branch</control> and <control>Trigger</control>.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            <control>Time range</control> offers <control>Last 7 days</control>, <control>Last 30 days</control>,
            <control>Last 90 days</control>, <control>Last 6 months</control> and <control>Last year</control>.
            <control>Pipeline</control>, <control>Branch</control> and <control>Trigger</control> accept several values;
            use <control>All</control> or <control>Clear</control> at the bottom of the popup.
            Click <control>Refresh</control> to reload the data.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Read the dashboard" id="dashboard-widgets">
        <p>The summary row shows:</p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Total Builds, Passed, Failed">Number of runs in the selected range.
                <control>Passed</control> includes partially succeeded runs.</def>
            <def title="Pass Rate">Share of runs that passed.</def>
            <def title="Avg Execution">Average run time from start to finish, without queue time, with the median below.</def>
            <def title="Avg Queue, Queue P95">Time runs waited for an agent: average and median, and the 95th percentile.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>The widgets below show:</p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Pipeline Pass Rate (%)">Pass rate over time.</def>
            <def title="Build Duration">Run duration over time.</def>
            <def title="Queue Time">Time spent waiting for an agent, over time.</def>
            <def title="Top Failing Pipelines">Pipelines with the most failures.
                Hidden when you filter on one pipeline.</def>
            <def title="Top Failure Causes">The most frequent failure reasons in a sample of failed runs.</def>
            <def title="Slowest Stages">Stages with the longest durations in a sample of runs.</def>
            <def title="Trigger Distribution">How runs were started, for example by CI, by a pull request or manually.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>To enlarge a widget, click its maximize button.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Agent pools" id="agent-pools">
        <p>
            The <control>Agents</control> tab lists the agent pools of the organization with the total number of agents
            and how many are online, busy and offline.
        </p>
        <procedure title="Inspect an agent pool" id="inspect-agent-pool">
            <step>
                <p>In the <control>Pipeline Metrics</control> editor tab, select the <control>Agents</control> tab.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Select a pool to open it.
                    The pool has three sub-tabs: <control>Details</control>, <control>Agents</control> and <control>Jobs</control>.</p>
                <img src="azd_agent_pools.png" alt="Agents tab with the agent pool list and one pool open on its Agents sub-tab" width="706" thumbnail="true" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            To narrow the pool list, click the filter icon and show pools by <control>Type</control>
            (<control>Self-hosted</control> or <control>Microsoft-hosted</control>) or by <control>Status</control>, or select <control>Favorites Only</control>.
            To sort it, click the sort icon and select <control>Name</control>, <control>Total agents</control>, <control>Online</control>,
            <control>Busy</control> or <control>Offline</control>.
        </p>
        <p>
            Mark the pools you use often with <control>Add to favorites</control>, so that <control>Favorites Only</control> shows only those.
            Double-click an agent or a job row to open its run.
            The run opens in the <control>AZD Pipelines</control> tool window, or in the browser if
            <a href="Azd-Settings-Configuration.topic" anchor="general-configuration">Open AZD links in tool window</a> is off.
        </p>

        <chapter title="Manage agents" id="manage-agents">
            <p>
                On the <control>Agents</control> sub-tab, select an agent and use the toolbar.
                These actions need the <control>Manage</control> permission on the pool; without it, the buttons stay disabled.
            </p>
            <deflist type="medium">
                <def title="Enable">The agent picks up new jobs again.</def>
                <def title="Disable for Maintenance">The agent finishes its current job and then takes no new work.</def>
                <def title="Rename…">Changes the agent name.</def>
                <def title="Edit Capabilities…">Adds, edits or removes user-defined capabilities.</def>
                <def title="Open in Browser">Opens the agent on Azure DevOps.</def>
            </deflist>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="If the dashboard is blank" id="metrics-jcef">
        <p>
            The dashboard uses the IDE built-in browser (JCEF).
            If JCEF is not available, the tab shows a message instead of the charts.
            See <a href="Azd-FAQ.topic" anchor="jcef-views">A view shows a message instead of content</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

